  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In the new CodeChef Learn module, under the \"Learn Problem Solving\" section, there are two courses for each language. For eg. \"Python Beginner - Part 1\" and \"Python Beginner - Part 2\". These courses help you get started with CodeChef contests.\n\nCurrently there are courses for 4 languages, and hence there are 8 courses in this section. But suppose there are courses for NNN languages, what will be the total number of courses in this section?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input will contain a single integer NNN, denoting the number of languages for which there are courses.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a single line the total number of courses in the section.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4",
        "output": "8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIf there are 444 languages, then there will be 2∗4=82 * 4 = 82∗4=8 courses in total."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "9",
        "output": "18",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIf there are 999 languages, then there will be 2∗9=182 * 9 = 182∗9=18 courses in total."
      }
    ]
  },
